<p>Meta said it plans to cut about 8,000 jobs, roughly 10% of its workforce, as it sharply ramps up spending on artificial intelligence and data centres. The company is racing with rivals including Amazon, Google, Microsoft and OpenAI in an expensive AI contest, and the Financial Times reported that Meta plans to spend about $135 billion on data centres this year. The move also fits a broader pullback across big tech as AI investment demands more cash. Microsoft is offering voluntary redundancy or buyouts to about 7% of its US staff, or roughly 8,750 people, in what several outlets described as the first programme of its kind for the company. Taken together, the announcements show how leading technology groups are redirecting money toward AI infrastructure, even as that shift brings painful job losses for thousands of workers.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/19qO9Sp1L1qUJ-vzhbgpwLJA-2azcrx9ThzXBTzT2gzqmBHQIFi_CZNZnVrJszbP6t7uoKYDrwP2Dm5E4Fddlv243yMqHusQqgt15WJEvXyJjLjfLlwchjpRLaVibkj8jwuithA-FxfH7UFahdMXkQ1F6z2cLptSjbNVjth0hoMSXy2zzGKAUc-HukzyVV3NyT12A8Yje1TRnZI6sgTKlv6LuuGNQT3Iv4u-QyvRD3drClXjxfe9LuQ' alt='A logo of Meta AI sits outside the Meta House on the opening day of the 55th annual meeting of the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, January 20, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Largest since: BBC said the cuts would be Meta&#x27;s biggest layoff round since 2023, and employees had been expecting the announcement for weeks.</li><li>Open vacancies: Alongside the layoffs, Meta is expected to leave thousands of other positions unfilled next month, according to AFP reporting cited by NDTV.</li><li>Microsoft scale: Microsoft is preparing to spend about $140 billion on AI investment this year while offering buyouts to long-serving US employees.</li><li>Sector pattern: Deutsche Welle and Semafor both described the Meta and Microsoft moves as part of an AI-fuelled reshaping of the wider US technology sector.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Meta leadership: Mark Zuckerberg is prioritizing the push toward superintelligence as Meta pours money into an AI race with other large technology groups. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/pixels/article/2026/04/23/meta-plans-layoffs-as-ai-spending-soars_6752761_13.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysis: The company is framing workforce cuts as a way to offset a huge jump in capital spending, with planned data-centre investment of about $135 billion this year. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/fe875f6c-f45c-4dbd-9d18-168d1fdbfd5f'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Microsoft: Microsoft is taking a voluntary approach to part of its workforce adjustment, offering redundancy packages to long-serving US employees rather than announcing matching compulsory layoffs in the cited reports. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/f5776fd6-22f3-43d1-806b-9858b64cfd18'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/pixels/article/2026/04/23/meta-plans-layoffs-as-ai-spending-soars_6752761_13.html'>Meta plans to lay off about 8,000 employees as AI spending soars</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/fe875f6c-f45c-4dbd-9d18-168d1fdbfd5f'>Meta to cut 10% of jobs to ‘offset’ Zuckerberg’s AI spending</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/meta-microsoft-purge-jobs-amid-ai-build-up/a-76918848'>Meta, Microsoft purge jobs amid AI build-up</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crm1y89vek8o'>Meta says it will cut 8,000 jobs as AI spending soars</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/23/2026/meta-microsoft-shrink-workforce-amid-ai-spending'>Meta, Microsoft shrink workforce amid AI spending</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/meta-to-layoff-10-workforce-amid-heavy-ai-investments-report-11400815#publisher=newsstand'>Meta To Lay Off 8,000 Employees Amid Heavy Investment In AI: Report</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='http